 "library": {
  "title": "Raspberry Pi 5 board, 85x56 mm, detailed",
  "description": "Like-for-like model of a Raspberry Pi 5 single-board computer for designing cases and checking fit. PCB 85 x 56 x 1.6 mm with 3 mm corner radius; origin at the PCB bottom-left corner, PCB underside at z=0, GPIO header along the top edge (y=56). Four M2.5 mounting holes (2.75 mm) at (3.5,3.5), (61.5,3.5), (3.5,52.5), (61.5,52.5). Right edge (x=85, ports overhang ~1.5 mm): Ethernet RJ45 at top (y 39.7-55.7, 13.5 high), stacked USB 3.0 in middle (y 21-35.7, 16 high, blue tongues), stacked USB 2.0 at bottom (y 2.5-17.2, 16 high). Bottom edge (y=0): USB-C power centred x=11.2, micro-HDMI 0 at x=25.8 and micro-HDMI 1 at x=39.2, two 22-pin MIPI CAM/DISP FPC connectors at x=45 and 52, UART and RTC battery headers. Left edge: PCIe FPC connector, power button, PWR/ACT LEDs; microSD socket and card on the underside protruding past x=0. Top: 2x20 GPIO header (pins 8.5 mm tall), BCM2712 SoC with heat spreader, LPDDR4X RAM, RP1, PMIC, Wi-Fi module can, 4-pin fan header, PoE+ header. Built from coloured primitives in sub-objects (PCB, GPIO, SoC, EdgePorts, Small, Underside). Not parametric; positions of the power button and FPC connectors are approximate. To use in a case, place the board with its underside on the standoff tops (e.g. z=5 for 3 mm standoffs on a 2 mm floor).",
